# Admin API scratchpad — VS Code REST Client (humao.rest-client).
# Run "login" first (click "Send Request" above it), then any call below reuses the token.
# Swap @baseUrl for the environment you're targeting; paste real credentials.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8010/v1
# @baseUrl = https://relab.example.org/v1   # staging/prod

# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/bearer/login
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

username=you@example.com&password=CHANGE_ME

###
# Token captured from the login response above.
# If your account has MFA, login returns an mfa-pending response instead of a
# token — skip it and hardcode a token grabbed from the app: @token = eyJ...
@token = {{login.response.body.access_token}}

## Cache -------------------------------------------------------------------

### Force-refresh the public stats (clears the cached /stats/* responses).
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/cache/clear/stats
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Clear any cache namespace: stats | reference-data | docs.
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/cache/clear/reference-data
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

## Users -------------------------------------------------------------------

### List users (paginated; add filters like ?email[ilike]=%acme.com).
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### View one user.
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/users/REPLACE_USER_ID
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Reset a locked-out user's MFA enrollment.
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/users/REPLACE_USER_ID/mfa/reset
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Delete a user (irreversible).
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/admin/users/REPLACE_USER_ID
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

## RPi cameras -------------------------------------------------------------

### List paired cameras.
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/plugins/rpi-cam/cameras
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Check a camera's online status.
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/plugins/rpi-cam/cameras/REPLACE_CAMERA_ID/status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

## Reference data ----------------------------------------------------------

### Create a taxonomy (only `name` is required).
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/taxonomies
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "New taxonomy",
  "description": "Created via admin.http"
}

### Create a category under a taxonomy (`name` + `taxonomy_id` for a root).
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "New category",
  "taxonomy_id": "REPLACE_TAXONOMY_ID"
}
